    rdfs1:comment "Lindsay Hunt is a South African hunter turned conservationist who played an important role in a project to produce Cape Buffalo breeding stock free of bovine tuberculosis and foot_and_mouth disease. This project has resulted in the establishing of disease_free herds in all nine provinces of South Africa, away from the TB_ravaged areas of the Kruger National Park."@en ;
