dbpedia:J._W._Gough dbo:abstract "John Wiedhofft Gough (23 February 1900 _ 1976) was a Welsh historian noted for his study of John Locke's political philosophy. Gough was described as an outstanding student whilst at Oxford, achieving a first in both the classics and modern history, in 1922 and 1923, respectively. He was a fellow of Oriel College, Oxford and in 1947 was appointed lecturer in modern history. He was awarded a DLitt in 1965."@en ;
    dbo:birthDate "1900_2_23"^^xsd:string ;
    dbo:deathDate "1976_0_0"^^xsd:string ;
