        yago:Worker109632518,
        yago:Writer110794014,
        yago:YagoLegalActor,
        yago:YagoLegalActorGeo,
        dbo:Person ;
    rdfs1:comment "Pere Marsili (also known as Peter Marsili) was a Dominican friar, chronicler, translator, and royal ambassador during the 13th and 14th centuries. In 1314 King James II of Aragon ordered him to make a Latin adaptation of a now_lost autobiography of James I of Aragon, the Llibre dels feyts. The Catalan language original famously recounted the heroics of James I, known as the \"Conqueror,\" and was a project in which the King himself had reputedly been involved. Marsili completed the four_part work in 1322 and titled it Commentarioum de gestis Regis Jacobi primi or Commentary on the Deeds of King James I (at times called the Liber gestorum or Book of Deeds, in reference to the original). Some historians believe he may also have written other extant works traditionally ascribed to a Pere Martel"@en,
        "Pedro Marsilio, (Pere Marsili en catalán) probablemente mallorquín, hermano de la orden de los predicadores, archidiácono del Obispado de Mallorca, cronista y embajador real al servicio del rey Jaime II de Aragón."@es ;
    rdfs1:label "Pere Marsili"@en,
        "Pedro Marsilio"@es ;
    owl:sameAs ns50:Pedro_Marsilio,
        <http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/m.0g9syw>,
        ns39:Q4889221,
        wikidata:Q4889221,
        ns38:Pere_Marsili ;
    ns44:wasDerivedFrom <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pere_Marsili?oldid=708608229> ;
    foaf:gender "male"@en ;
    foaf:givenName "Pedro"@en ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf ns46:Pere_Marsili ;
    foaf:name "Pere Marsili"@en .

dbpedia:Peter_Bucher dbo:abstract "Peter Bucher (born April 3, 1947) is a former West German handball player who competed in the 1972 Summer Olympics. In 1972 he was part of the West German team which finished sixth in the Olympic tournament. He played all six matches and scored twenty goals."@en ;
