dbpedia:Jack_Collom dbo:abstract "Jack Collom (born November 8, 1931 in Chicago, Illinois) is an American poet, teacher and essayist. His twenty_five books include Blue Heron & IBC, The Fox, Arguing with Something Plato Said, Red Car Goes By: Selected Poems 1955_2000, Exchanges of Earth and Sky and Situation Sings (with Lyn Hejinian). His latest book of poems, Second Nature, won the 2013 Colorado Book Award for Poetry. He has been anthologized in countless magazines and collections in the United States and abroad, from Best Poems of 1963 to The Best American Poetry 2004."@en ;
