dbpedia:Lisy_Fischer dbo:abstract "Elisabeth (Lisy) Fischer (born 22 August 1900 in Zurich, Switzerland – died 6 June 1999 in Newcastle upon Tyne, England) was a talented pianist from a talented Jewish family. Born to parents Arthur Fischer (from Deutsch Eylau, Prussia _ now Iława, Poland) and Bertha Hochstetter (from Liedolsheim, Germany), she was a child prodigy giving piano recitals from 11 years of age first in Geneva and afterwards in Paris under the tutelage of Lucien Grou de Flagny and later Charles Barbier."@en ;
