dbpedia:Armstrong_Pame dbo:abstract "Armstrong Pame is an officer in the Indian Administrative Service. He is the first IAS officer from Zeme Tribe of the Naga Peoples. Pame belongs to Tamenglong district of Manipur. After completing his bachelor's degree from St.Stephens College in 2005 he appeared from UPSC Indian Revenue service Exam. After clearing the UPSC exam in 2008, he was selected for Indian Administrative Service(IAS). He is acclaimed for building a 100 km road famously known as the \"Peoples' Road\" connecting Manipur to Nagaland and Assam. In August 2012, he raised INR40 Lakh for this purpose through Facebook page. For his efforts in building road with donation and volunteers he was invited to Facebook headquarters in California In 2012, he was nominated for CNN_IBN Indian of the Year in Public service category."@en ;
    dbo:wikiPageID 47014066 ;
    dbo:wikiPageRevisionID 738426630 ;
