dbpedia:Gianni_Bongioanni dbo:abstract "Gianni Bongioanni (* 1928 in Turin) ist ein italienischer Regisseur."@de,
        "Giovanni (Gianni) Bongioanni (born August 6, 1921 in Turin) is an Italian film director, screenwriter, cinematographer, camera operator, editor, writer and occasional actor. He was one of the earliest directors to adopt an authentic, neo_realistic approach to Italian film_making, and his film La svolta pericolosa (1959) is considered the first Italian television series. In addition, Bongioanni was actively involved in the Italian TV and radio broadcasting industries, in which he worked for several years before making his first feature film, Tre per una rapina (1964)."@en ;
    dbo:birthDate "1928_1_1"^^xsd:string ;
