dbpedia:Hege_Storhaug dbo:abstract "Hege Storhaug  (born 21 May 1962) is a Norwegian journalist, author and political activist. She has been noted since the 1990s for her criticism of Islam and immigration, and for her women's rights activism, highlighting Muslim women in particular. Since 2002, she has been the information director of Human Rights Service, a foundation she co_founded with Rita Karlsen. Formerly an active volleyball player, Storhaug is a certified athletic trainer with a degree from the Norwegian School of Sport Sciences, and has highlighted eating disorders among female athletes. She has played on the Norwegian women's national volleyball team, and coached and played on teams that have won the Norwegian national championships."@en ;
