dbpedia:Jean_Jacques_Mandrichi ns70:height "184.0"^^ns69:centimetre ;
    dbo:abstract "Jean_Jacques Mandrichi (born June 3, 1984 in Bastia) is a French football striker. He currently plays for CA Bastia. After a successful time at AC Ajaccio Mandrichi signed a two_year deal to play for Grenoble Foot 38. On 30 July 2011, he moved to Ligue 2 rivals FC Nantes, signing a two_year contract. Soon after the signing, the player was openly criticized by club owner Waldemar Kita, and on October 4, 2011, FC Nantes and Jean_Jacques Mandrichi decided to terminate the contract signed in late July. He signed a 2 years contract with LB Châteauroux, but after one season, he moved to newly promoted Ligue 2 side Gazélec Ajaccio on a 2_year deal. In January 2013, Mandrichi moved to Championnat National side Red Star Saint_Ouen."@en,
        "Jean_Jacques Mandrichi est un footballeur français né le 3 juin 1984 à Bastia, évoluant au poste d'attaquant à l'AS Cannes."@fr ;
    dbo:birthDate "1984_06_03"^^xsd:string,
