dbpedia:Rhys_Pollock ns70:height "184.0"^^ns69:centimetre ;
    dbo:abstract "Rhys Pollock (* 14. März 1980 in Sydney) ist ein australischer Radrennfahrer."@de,
        "Rhys Pollock (born 14 March 1980) is an Australian racing cyclist and former national under_23 MTB champion. Pollock has ridden as a professional since 2005 for continental teams from Asia, Europe and Australia. In 2005 he was a member of the Marco Polo and has gone on to ride for DFL_Cyclingnews_Litespeed and Drapac Professional Cycling. A bad weather specialist, Pollock has had wins in Australia's longest one day race, Melbourne to Warrnambool and stage 2, 2011 Tour of Tasmania when it snowed."@en,
        "Rhys Pollock, né le 14 mars 1980 à Sydney, est un coureur cycliste australien."@fr,
        "Rhys Pollock (Sydney, 14 maart 1980) is een Australisch wielrenner die anno 2014 uitkomt voor ChasterMason Giant Racing. Na eerder te hebben gereden voor het Marco Polo Cyclingteam, DFL_Cyclingnews_Litespeed en Drapac Cycling."@nl ;
