dbpedia:Annæus_Johannes_Schjødt dbo:abstract "Annæus Johannes Schjødt (3 July 1830 – 7 July 1893) was a Norwegian barrister. He was born in Christiania to Simon Peter Schjødt and Andrea Emilie Schriver. He was married to Laura Marie Rømcke from 1885 to 1892, and to writer Edle Hartmann from 1900. He was the father of jurist Annæus Schjødt. Schjødt was barrister with access to work with the Supreme Court from 1885. He was member of the Storting from 1894 to 1900. He served as Attorney General of Norway from 1917. He was decorated Knight of the Order of St. Olav in 1910."@en ;
