dbpedia:Bill_Dalley ns70:height "163.0"^^ns69:centimetre ;
    ns70:weight "63.0"^^ns69:kilogram ;
    dbo:abstract "William Charles \"Bill\" Dalley (18 November 1901 – 9 February 1989) was a New Zealand rugby union player. Starting out as a utility back, Dalley made his debut at a provincial level for Canterbury in 1921. He became a specialist halfback in 1924, and was quickly selected for the New Zealand national side, the All Blacks, that year. Between then and 1929 he played 35 matches for the All Blacks including five internationals. He captained the side in his final two appearances in 1929. In all he scored five tries for the All Blacks. After retiring as a player, Dalley served as a member of the Canterbury Rugby Union's management committee from 1932 to 1955, the last three years as chairman."@en,
        "William (Bill) Charles Dalley, né le 18 novembre 1901 à Lyttelton (Nouvelle_Zélande) et décédé le 9 février 1989 à Christchurch, est un joueur de rugby à XV qui a joué avec l'équipe de Nouvelle_Zélande. Il évoluait au poste de demi de mêlée (1,63 m pour 63 kg)."@fr ;
