dbpedia:Carlos_García_y_García dbo:abstract "Carlos García y García (? – May 10, 2016) was a Peruvian politician and Baptist pastor. García y García served as Second Vice President of Peru from 1990 to 1992 during the administration of President Alberto Fujimori. Though García y García was a member of Fujimori's Change 90 political party, he publicly condemned Fujimori's coup and constitutional crisis, which took place on April 5, 1992. García y García, a Baptist minister, also served as the President of the National Evangelical Council (Concilio Nacional Evangélico). In July 2002, García y García was awarded the Medalla de Honor del Congreso (Grand Officer) for his defense of democracy and the Constitution during the 1992 Peruvian constitutional crisis. Carlos García y García died on May 10, 2016. His wake and viewing was held at a church in the Lince District of Lima on May 12, 2016."@en,
        "Carlos García y García (?_10 de mayo de 2016) fue un pastor evangélico y político peruano. Fue segundo vicepresidente de la República durante el primer gobierno de Alberto Fujimori (1990_1992)."@es ;
