    rdfs1:comment "Henryk Budziński (November 29, 1904 – March 18, 1983) was a Polish rower who competed in the 1932 Summer Olympics. In 1932 he won the bronze medal with his partner Jan Krenz_Mikołajczak in the coxless pairs event. He was born in Bobryk, Baranovichi and died in Gdańsk."@en,
        "Henryk Budziński (ur. 29 listopada 1904 w Bobryku koło Stanisławowa, zm. 18 marca 1983 w Gdańsku) – polski wioślarz, medalista olimpijski."@pl ;
