dbpedia:Jacob_Eason ns70:weight "106.596"^^ns69:kilogram ;
    dbo:abstract "Jacob Eason (born November 17, 1997) is an American football quarterback. He is enrolled at the University of Georgia and is playing college football. Eason attended Lake Stevens High School in Lake Stevens, Washington. As a sophomore, he passed for 2,941 yards and 23 touchdowns. As a junior in 2014, he was Rivals.com's Junior of the Year after passing for 2,829 yards, 32 touchdowns and three interceptions. Eason is rated by Rivals as a five_star recruit and is ranked as the best pro_style quarterback and best player overall in the 2016 class. Eason committed to the University of Georgia to play college football. His father, Tony Eason, played college football at the University of Notre Dame, but is not the Tony Eason who played for the New England Patriots."@en ;
