dbpedia:John_Cleve_Green dbo:abstract "John Cleve Green (April 14, 1800 – April 29, 1875) was a merchant and former partner of John Murray Forbes in the China trading house of Russell & Company. Green was a major benefactor of Princeton University and the Lawrenceville School, giving upwards of 1.5 million dollars, perhaps 2 million, to Princeton On his death he also made major bequests to New York University and New York area hospitals."@en ;
