dbpedia:Peadar_Maher dbo:abstract "Peadar Maher (1 February 1924 – 31 January 2012) was an Irish Fianna Fáil politician who served as a Teachta Dála (TD) for the Laois–Offaly constituency. A publican by profession, Maher was first elected to Dáil Éireann at the 1951 general election and held his seat until retiring at the 1961 general election. He died in 2012."@en ;
    dbo:birthDate "1924_2_1"^^xsd:string ;
    dbo:deathDate "2012_1_31"^^xsd:string ;
