dbpedia:Jaume_Serra_i_Cau dbo:abstract "Jaume Serra i Cau (Valencian pronunciation: [ˈdʒawme ˈsɛra j ˈkaw], Spanish: Jaime Serra y Cau) (died 1517) was a Spanish Valencian cardinal, from the city of Valencia. He was tutor to the young Giovanni Borgia, and a close associate of his father Pope Alexander VI. He was archbishop of Oristano in 1492, and was created Cardinal in 1500. He was bishop of Linköping in 1501, bishop of Elne in 1506. He was bishop of Albano in 1511, and possibly bishop of Palestrina in 1516 (sources disagree). He was Governor of Rome, and Governor of Cesena He was buried in San Giacomo degli Spagnoli, where a mortuary chapel was built for him."@en,
        "Jaime Serra i Cau (A veces llamado Jaume), (Valencia, 1427...1430 _ Roma 15 de marzo de 1517), Cardenal español."@es,
        "Jaime Serra i Cau (né à Valence, Espagne, vers 1427/1430, et mort à Rome le 15 mars 1517) est un cardinal espagnol du XVIe siècle et du début XVIe siècle."@fr ;
    dbo:birthDate "1427_0_0"^^xsd:string ;
    dbo:birthPlace dbpedia:Valencia ;
    dbo:deathDate "1517_0_0"^^xsd:string ;
    dbo:deathPlace dbpedia:Rome ;
    dbo:wikiPageExternalLink "http://www.fiu.edu/~mirandas/bios1500_ii.htm" ;
