dbpedia:Víctor_Pons dbo:abstract "Víctor Pons (April 5, 1935_November 11, 1999) was a former Chief Justice of the Supreme Court of Puerto Rico and Secretary of State of Puerto Rico. Born in Rio Piedras, Puerto Rico, he was appointed by Governor Rafael Hernández Colón, Pons headed the high court from 1985 until 1992, succeeding Chief Justice José Trías Monge. A prominent private sector attorney, Pons managed Hernández Colón's electoral campaigns before holding public office."@en ;
