dbpedia:Jim_English dbo:abstract "James \"Jim\" English (October 1932 – 23 February 2008) was an Irish hurler who played as a right wing_back for the Wexford senior team. English joined the team during the 1951 championship and subsequently became a regular member of the starting fifteen until his retirement after the 1964 championship. During that time he won three All_Ireland medals, five Leinster medals and two National Hurling League medals. In 1956 English captained the team to the All_Ireland title. At club level English enjoyed a successful career with Rathnure in Wexford and later with Erin's Own in Carlow. He won numerous club championship winners' medals in both codes."@en ;
