dbpedia:Rosita_Arenas dbo:abstract "Rosa \"Rosita\" Arenas (born 19 August 1933) is a Mexican actress whose film career was most prominent during the 1950s and 1960s. She was born in Caracas, Venezuela, the daughter of Spanish actor Miguel Arenas. At age 16, she was named Reina de la Primavera (Queen of the Spring), and subsequently made her film debut in Anacleto se divorcia (1950). She received more important roles in ¡¿Qué te ha dado esa mujer?! (1951), with Pedro Infante and Luis Aguilar, and El señor fotógrafo (1953), with Cantinflas. She also tried her hand at singing; in Los chiflados del rock and roll (1957), she sang the songs \"Se me hizo fácil\", \"Serenata huasteca\", and \"Qué manera de perder\"."@en,
        "Rosita Arenas (Caracas, Venezuela, 19 de agosto de 1933) es una actriz mexicana nacida en Venezuela, trabajó en el cine mexicano, español e italiano. Recordada por haber hecho películas consideradas como clásicos dentro de la industria cinematográfica mexicana. Actualmente se encuentra retirada."@es ;
