dbpedia:Ibrahima_Bangoura ns70:height "180.0"^^ns69:centimetre ;
    dbo:abstract "Ibrahima Sory Bangoura (born 8 December 1982 in Conakry) is a Guinean footballer who last played in Spain for CP Cacereño. Bangoura was a member of the Guinea squad for the 2006 African Nations Cup, where the team was eliminated in the quarter_finals. His cousin Ismaël Bangoura is also a footballer and a member of the team. His favourite position is second striker although he has played as winger or as an attacking midfielder. He is well known for his pace."@en,
        "Ibrahim Bangoura est un footballeur professionnel originaire de Guinée évoluant au poste d'attaquant dans le club de Denizlispor. Il joue également dans l'équipe de Guinée de football. Né le 8 décembre 1982 à Conakry en République de Guinée, il mesure 1,72 m pour 72 kg."@fr,
        "Ibrahima Bangoura (ur. 8 grudnia 1982 w Konakry) – gwinejski piłkarz grający na pozycji napastnika. Obecnie występuje w tureckim Denizlisporze."@pl ;
