dbpedia:Jo_Hee_bong dbo:abstract "Jo Hee_bong (born August 23, 1971) is a South Korean actor. Jo began his acting career in 1997 as part of the theatre troupe Bipa (비파). He later became known as a supporting actor onscreen, in films such as Blind (2011) and Incomplete Life: Prequel (2013), and the television dramas Hong Gil_dong (2008), Joseon X_Files (2010), and Good Doctor (2013). In a collaboration with director Kim Tae_yong, Jo is also the live narrator (or byeonsa) for Crossroads of Youth (1934), Korea's oldest surviving silent film. Aside from local performances in 2008 and 2012, Jo has performed at the 2009 New York Film Festival, the 2011 Guwahati International Film Festival in Mexico, the 2011 Thames Festival in London, and the 2013 Berlin International Film Festival."@en,
        "曹熙奉（朝鮮語：조희봉，1971年8月23日－），韓國男演員。"@zh ;
